etch a possible graph of a function $f(x)$ that satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- $f'(3)=0$\n- if $x \\in (-\\infty,3)$ then $f'(x)> 0$\n- if $x \\in (3,+\\infty)$ then $f'(x)<0$\n- $f''(x) < 0$ for all $x \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n\nWe summarize all the given information in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty,3)$ | $3$ | $(3,\\infty)$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f'$ | $+$ | $0$ | $-$ |\n| $f''$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $f$ | $\\nearrow\\:\\:\\frown$ | $\\textrm{max}$ | $\\searrow\\:\\:\\frown$ |\n\nNow, let's sketch our graph:\n\n- We draw a point on the vertical line $x=3$, where the tangent to the graph is horizontal.\n- Since $x=3$ is a local maximum, the graph must go down to the left and to the right of that point.\n- Finally, the graph must be concave down everywhere.\n\nTherefore, a possible graph of $f$ is as follows:\n\n![](images/7c/7c6d8412e9c657e8e4a148e40ca0b8a073735d3b88681eec6a79f763471aaf4f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1065 655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7f1b863e-e172-5e84-8f8d-1ea21025605d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102007 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186507591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1045 "Sketching a Function Given Some Derivative Properties" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186507588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506670 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050544 #e